  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "version-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Version drift: appinfo/info.xml says 0.47.0, package.json says 0.1.0.",
        "  The App Store and the server read info.xml; everything on the node side reads package.json. Whichever is behind, a release ends up carrying two version numbers, and only one of them reaches the user."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "php-extensions",
      "lines": [
        "1 PHP extension is required by composer but not listed as <lib> in appinfo/info.xml:",
        "  iconv (prinsfrank/pdfparser, symfony/polyfill-mbstring)",
        "  A Nextcloud server need not load it. The server checks <lib> before it enables the app; composer only checks where it runs. Without the <lib> the app is enabled anyway and the first call into the extension fails at runtime."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is vereinsbuchhaltung, the checkout directory is nc_vereinsbuchhaltung.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support-max",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml caps PHP at max-version 8.5.",
        "  A server on a newer PHP refuses to enable the app, so this cap has to be raised deliberately with every PHP release, not left where it was."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (eslint.config.mjs), Stylelint (stylelint.config.cjs), PHPUnit (phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php).",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence agpl (appinfo/info.xml), AGPL-3.0-or-later (package.json, composer.json).",
        "  agpl in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. With min-version 33 info.xml can state an SPDX id instead.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "repository-link",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml links its repository and its bug tracker."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "link-dead",
